  Cell["4. Archimedean reduction", "Section"], Cell["Source: 4.qmgrobnertest.nb. Proposition 4.1, \
p. 18; also used in 4.2. The substitutions use the coefficient conditions of Proposition 4.1 \
together with the quaternion hypothesis. After the initial conditions other than b12=b21=0, the \
polynomial is 2 l n (b12+(a11-a22)r)(b21-(a11-a22)r)-t1. Its l n r^2 coefficient is -2(a11-a22)^2, \
so vanishing gives a11=a22=u before this reduction. Then M=u I4+N with N^2=0. Since alpha_s=i_s has \
square kappa in Q\\{0}, M^2=kappa I4 gives u^2=kappa and 2u b12=2u b21=0; hence b12=b21=0. This \
deduction precedes the reduction. The reduction keeps a11,a22 symbolic. The replacement rules do \
not assign values to the parameters.", "Text"], 
